# Branching & Production-Architecture Guard

For all website feature work, use the current [Branching, Integration and Release Workflow](../../docs/development/BRANCHING_INTEGRATION_RELEASE.md). For the current homepage read the [Four-Frame Handoff](../../docs/genezisi-v2/HANDOFF_2026-11-01_FOUR_FRAME.md).

1. Never assume the chat's stored SHA is the current branch head. Inspect live `main`, open PRs and the intended target before writing.
2. **No feature-per-edit branching.** Keep related changes on their existing coherent task branch. Independent features branch from current `main`; dependent tasks branch from the current integration branch. A release integration branch starts from `main` and is kept synchronized with new `main` changes.
3. Build **shipping code in the real Next.js/React/TypeScript app** (including locale routing and existing CSS/JS contracts). Standalone HTML studies and proofs remain non-production references unless explicitly converted. Never call them ready-to-merge implementations.
4. Push work to non-production branches; use a draft PR early. Do not merge old experimental history or cherry-pick everything. Keep diffs scoped and development deployments economical.
5. The automated gate must include the actual app's typecheck, build, pertinent tests and where possible runtime/browser checks for DOM visibility, motion, navigation, cache/coherency, reverse scroll, reduced motion and locales. Mark unrun checks **not run**, never "passed".
6. A successful build or source-level test ≠ founder approval. Founder owns actual visual acceptance. Final merge to `main` requires explicit approval for the integrated version, not the standalone proof.
7. For the current hero, preserve the accepted Card 1–4 art direction and V6.5 shortcut unless instructed otherwise. Check PR #19's Card 3 visibility fix in a real browser before claiming it resolved.
